# Pending backend UI

When the UI is waiting on the server (save, API, MCP-backed persist, catalog write), **show a spinner on the control or section that triggered the wait** — do not leave the surface looking idle.

## Do

- Put `aria-busy` on the pending control/section; disable re-entry while in flight.
- Prefer a local spinner on the clicked control (checkbox, cargo tile, quantum row, button). For multi-field cards, also mark the row/section busy.
- Use the shared `Spinner` from `components/ui/Spinner.tsx` (Storybook **Primitives/Spinner**).
- Await / `.finally` the persist Promise so pending clears on success and failure.
- Keep optimistic UI if already used; the spinner means “echo not confirmed yet,” not “blocked forever.”

## Don’t

- Rely only on a global page spinner for trip-table edits.
- Leave sticky toolbar / stop cards with no feedback while `saveChecklist` (or similar) runs.
- Invent one-off spinner SVGs in feature files — extend `Spinner` if needed.

## Trip checklist (canonical)

| Action | Pending cue |
| --- | --- |
| Mark stop done | Checkbox / Mark complete control |
| Cargo handled tile | That tile |
| Quantum insert / retarget | Quantum row (and composer confirm) |
| Any in-flight session save | Subtle sticky-toolbar “Saving…” |

Same rule applies to modals and catalog writes that mutate live session state.
